 host VM kernel is updated or boots without `systemd.unified_cgroup_hier) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 575 Td (       > archy=0`, Isolate initialization will immediately fail. Gate G1 and G2 in `v) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 564.5 Td (       > erify-cgroups-isolate.sh` enforce this before activation.) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 554 Td ( 112 | 2. **Container Privileged Mode:**) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 543.5 Td ( 113 |    `judge0-workers` operates with `privileged: true` to manage mount namespaces ) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 533 Td (       > and host cgroups. Although untrusted code runs as an unprivileged UID \(`6000) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 522.5 Td (       > 0+`\) inside Isolate, an unpatched Linux kernel vulnerability could theoretic) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 512 Td (       > ally permit container breakout. Single-tenancy on the runner VM is the criti) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 501.5 Td (       > cal compensating control.) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 491 Td ( 114 | 3. **APT Package Version Drift:**) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 480.5 Td ( 115 |    While OpenSSL and Ruby source downloads are cryptographically pinned via SHA-) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 470 Td (       > 256, OS packages \(`gcc`, `openjdk-17-jdk-headless`, `nodejs`\) are installed ) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 459.5 Td (       > via `apt-get` from Ubuntu and NodeSource mirrors. Minor revision updates to ) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 449 Td (       > these distribution packages could occur over time.) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 438.5 Td ( 116 | 4. **Staging Concurrency Bound:**) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 428 Td ( 117 |    Because Isolate child processes are sibling-accounted, increasing concurrency) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 417.5 Td (       >  \(`COUNT > 1`\) in the future will require re-evaluating the physical memory ) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 407 Td (       > budget to prevent host-level OOM events.) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 396.5 Td ( 118 | ) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 386 Td ( 119 | ---) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 375.5 Td ( 120 | ) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 365 Td ( 121 | ## 6. Next Authorized Action on ARM64 Host) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 354.5 Td ( 122 | ) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 344 Td ( 123 | The repository changes are verified. When authorized by the infrastructure team,) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 333.5 Td (       >  the operator may proceed on the dedicated Azure ARM64 VM with the following) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 323 Td (       >  command sequence:) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 312.5 Td ( 124 | ) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 302 Td ( 125 | ```bash) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 291.5 Td ( 126 | # 1. Pull latest repository changes) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 281 Td ( 127 | cd /opt/testforge) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 270.5 Td ( 128 | git pull origin main) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 260 Td ( 129 | ) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 249.5 Td ( 130 | # 2. Build native ARM64 container images \(Bypass emulation\)) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 239 Td ( 131 | cd /opt/testforge/deploy/judge0) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 228.5 Td ( 132 | sudo bash build-arm64.sh) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 218 Td ( 133 | ) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 207.5 Td ( 134 | # 3. Verify ELF binary architectures and toolchains) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 197 Td ( 135 | sudo bash verify-arm64-binaries.sh) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 186.5 Td ( 136 | ) Tj ET BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 40 176 Td ( 137 | # 4. Deploy container stack with verified ARM64 images